Z||000006||GTFiero1||10-22-2001||10:29 PM||||i started off with a small fish tank, much easier for a begginer, when i up graded to a 12 gallon i had many problems, the biggest one i found is after i filled it completely up with everthing including fish and i found out a has a leak on the bottom, major pain in the @$$ before you set up your fish tank, take it out side and fill it with some water with a hose first to test for leaks. i have a 15 gallon tank now. its a good size tank, i bought it for 120 bucks with the Marineland system, its one complete unit that sits on the top.then something struck my tank and killed all my fish within a matter of months (never had this the 3 years before i owned fish)i cleaned it out well and put new fish in it and they still died except one that lived through both times. actually this happened to me right before i got my new one with my old 10gal tank. i got rid of all my fish and have 4 snapper turtles now but i need i new filtration system for that. go to <A HREF="http://www.marineland.co" TARGET=_blank>www.marineland.co</A>  (i think) i need some dort of under gravel filter for my turtles though, any one know of one that the water only need to be a few inches high to work?<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
